From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: quantforge-br <218010578+quantforge-br@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: don't count hangs on the shared VM

On targets without per-process page tables (A5xx, e.g. the A530 in
MSM8996) every DRM file gets gpu->vm.  recover_worker() increments
vm->faults for the guilty submit, and MSM_PARAM_FAULTS returns
global_faults + vm->faults, so one process hanging the GPU changes the
value every other process reads.  Mesa's freedreno turns that into
GL_INNOCENT_CONTEXT_RESET for every robust context, and compositors that
cannot recreate their context abort: Hyprland 0.57 does exactly that
("glGetGraphicsResetStatus returned GL_INNOCENT_CONTEXT_RESET. Cannot
continue until proper GPU reset handling is implemented.") whenever a
browser's GPU process hangs the A530.

Skip the VM count when the submit used the shared gpu->vm.  The guilty
context still sees its submitqueue fault count change (GUILTY reset),
and innocent contexts, whose submits are replayed after recovery, see
no reset, which is what targets with private VMs already do.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
index bf9109a..bcc4152 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -494,7 +494,16 @@ static void recover_worker(struct kthread_work *work)
 	else {
 		struct msm_gem_vm *vm = to_msm_vm(submit->vm);
 
-		vm->faults++;
+		/*
+		 * Without per-process page tables every context shares
+		 * gpu->vm, so counting the hang on the VM would make
+		 * MSM_PARAM_FAULTS change for every process and report an
+		 * innocent context reset to all of them.  The submitqueue
+		 * count above still tells the guilty context, the same as on
+		 * targets with private VMs.
+		 */
+		if (!(gpu->vm_shared && submit->vm == gpu->vm))
+			vm->faults++;
 
 		/*
 		 * If userspace has opted-in to VM_BIND (and therefore userspace
-- 
